            {
                "entry_id": "16ff3573-e669-3692-b454-64634ba2590d",
                "word": "ne",
                "pos": "conj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                        "entry_id": "16ff3573-e669-3692-b454-64634ba2590d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d6f64a2-ed41-4879-8dfb-dd797cb6a017",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "That than I shall not geve therunto faith ne credence, nor therfore put them to any maner ponyssement, before that they or any of them so accused may be at their lawful defence and answer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b92abbbd-04b7-430d-b28b-f5f700589aeb",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "And therin is no drede nor bytternes ne expences, but therin is pure recreacyon of body and of soule soo it be donn in clene places."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38b586f8-6ac6-4489-9731-9075d22da2bd",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Be not to hasty ne sodenly vengeable, to poure folke doo no vyolence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "653e442e-b357-4422-b8c8-0216f147df3d",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Moreouer no man be so hardy to drynk fastyng cold water, ne after that he hath accompanyed wyth a woman, ne after gret trauayle, ne after exersice tyll he haue fyrst rested hym, ne by nyght namely yf he haue do gloue tofore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5baa31d6-efea-47f2-87ff-22da9ce3944e",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "A false tonge wyll euer Imagyne and saye / That neuer by creature was sayd ne thought."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44a85a27-6ac4-4b6e-8c89-03289686e3a8",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "For chastyce can he not by daye ne nyght his wyfe but by his betynge maketh lyght and hote the loue bytwene her and her frende."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "699c52f4-2044-4dca-b7ff-4d7611c66eb1",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Item, that noo woman nor maide weyve any worsted stamynges ne sayes for that that thei be nott of sufficient powre to werke the said worsteddes as thei owte to be wrought, upon payne of iij s iiij d as often as thei be founde wevyng to be devyded and leuyed in maner and forme aboue expressed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe89b0cc-7876-43c5-aa3e-681758e939f8",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "That they shulde no lenger kepe ne susteyne Thomas the archebysshope."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d2a6d32-538c-4aac-a176-cc39dd8c0c12",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "The rote ought to be gadered in the begynnynge of somer and dryed in the sonne bycause [tha]¬t it corrupt ne rotte bycause of the moystnesse[,] & it may be kept two yeres;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d62ba28b-3164-4d44-bdcd-a47318a8eb30",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "For lyinge is a detestable vice, and to be hated of all men, ne to be suffred amonge seruantis ne other persones[,] howe poure estate so euer they be of."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2206deb-a227-4b98-a24a-d47d6aa9b60c",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Thus some persones beeyng inuited and exhorted to falle to the studie of lettres, make their excuse that thei bee sickely, that thei can not slepe ne take their naturall reste in the nightes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afd2848c-b963-4afc-831e-9c470bc8e0e3",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "We Moores be not so base of wit, ne yet so blunt of mynd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9ffdeb5-16c0-41d9-aa4f-124ee65f0f2a",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "The deuyll gossyp, ought me a shame / And prayde I am nowe, euerye penye I wolde god he had, be blinde and lame / The daye and houre, he fyrste woed me / Ware not gossyp, these chyldren thre I wolde not tary, ye may be sure / Longer with hym, daye ne houre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3808db5d-9e15-464e-9b6a-98f84b44d208",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Neither extremitie, ne gentle meanes could boote; she hydeth close within her brest, her secret sorowes roote."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "658bdba6-8436-462d-9c69-2468b14fd0a2",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Ne on her teares or plaint, at all to have remorse, but (if they can not with her will,) to bring the mayde perforce."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e825283-eb2e-4010-8838-2aea41e0a7ce",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "His hart encreaseth not thereby ne lesseth as edoon these fooles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a167627-9287-4e44-8d5e-4c13954beb57",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "And that no victualer ne other person or persons forestall any kynde of victualls cominge to the said Cyty or within the precyncte of the same before the same victualls be come to the place."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d53cdf0-f2a8-4a29-ac9b-eed7131ba2b4",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Ioc: How can that be and thou my ioy in warre? Po: Henceforth n'am I your ioy ne yet your sonne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2525ee8e-e689-4504-9b7c-98b3389b5328",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "But to her cry they list not lenden eare, / Ne ought the more their mightie strokes surceasse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa41f652-bd1f-4d8c-88d1-7a231a737117",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "Whose worth all outward is in shew alone / But inward sent hath not, ne vertue none."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c2c9067-406c-4b20-b812-8fa255ce06cf",
                                "sense_id": "72bfb882-01fb-32bf-9706-fdb32072605a",
                                "text": "The pang, the curse, with which they died, / Had never pass'd away; / I could not draw my een from theirs / Ne turn them up to pray."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
